# 💬 Local Ollama Chatbot

A ChatGPT-like AI chatbot built using **Streamlit**, **FastAPI**, **Ollama**, and **SQLite**. The application supports multiple chat sessions with persistent chat history and streams responses from locally running LLMs such as **Llama 3**.

---

## 🚀 Features

- 🤖 Chat with locally running Ollama models
- 💬 ChatGPT-style user interface
- ⚡ Real-time streaming responses
- 🗂️ Persistent multi-chat history
- 🗑️ Delete chat sessions
- 🌡️ Adjustable temperature
- 🧠 Custom system prompt
- 📦 SQLite database for chat storage
- 🔄 FastAPI backend
- 🎨 Streamlit frontend

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
|------------|---------|
| Python | Programming Language |
| Streamlit | Frontend UI |
| FastAPI | Backend API |
| Ollama | Local LLM Runtime |
| Llama 3 | Large Language Model |
| SQLite | Chat History Database |
| Requests | API Communication |
| HTTPX | Async HTTP Client |
| Pydantic | Data Validation |

---

## 📂 Project Structure

```
Cockroaches/
│
├── backend.py          # FastAPI backend
├── frontend.py         # Streamlit frontend
├── db.py               # SQLite database functions
├── chat_history.db     # Chat history database
├── requirements.txt
├── README.md
```

---

## ⚙️ Requirements

- Python 3.10+
- Ollama
- Llama 3 or Llama 3.2 model

---

## 📥 Installation

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/om22310858-cloud/Cockroaches.git
cd Cockroaches
```

---

### 2. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

### 3. Install Ollama

Download from

https://ollama.com/download

---

### 4. Pull a model

```bash
ollama pull llama3
```

or

```bash
ollama pull llama3.2
```

---

### 5. Start Ollama

```bash
ollama serve
```

---

### 6. Start the FastAPI backend

```bash
uvicorn backend:app --reload --port 8000
```

Backend API

```
http://localhost:8000
```

Swagger Documentation

```
http://localhost:8000/docs
```

---

### 7. Start Streamlit

```bash
streamlit run frontend.py
```

Open

```
http://localhost:8501
```

